# BUGS

A group holds at most 1024 variables among all groups, each up to 1 MiB, and `envd` 32 MiB of values in all; there are at most 128 groups.
A child whose parent exits before the child first touches `/env` finds the group gone, and gets a new one filled from its `env=` records.
rc(1) writes a variable to `/env` only when it starts a program, not as it is assigned, and does not remove one it deletes.
`envd` is restarted if it exits, but the groups are gone with it.
